--TEST--
Core\Task::afterResponse defers a callable past the end of the request body and runs the queue in registration order, which is what register_shutdown_function does — the two members a program reaches for to answer a client and keep working — `rule:concurrency/after-response-outlives-the-connection`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// PHP's `fastcgi_finish_request` is the member with this member's *name*, and
// it is not the twin: it flushes and detaches, taking no callback and existing
// under no SAPI a test can run, so a program that wants work after the response
// writes `fastcgi_finish_request()` and then keeps executing — or, under every
// other SAPI, registers a shutdown function. `register_shutdown_function` is
// therefore what this is measured against: the same claim about *when*, minus
// the response, which a CLI run does not have. `nvs_runtime::deferred` is the
// one home for what "after the response" means on a host that has one.
echo "response written\n";

// Two registrations, and the request goes on running between them. A member
// that ran the callable where it was registered would interleave these lines
// with the body's, and one that only stored it would print neither.
Core\Task::afterResponse(fn (): void => {
    echo "1 receipt\n";
});
Core\Task::afterResponse(fn (): void => {
    echo "2 webhook\n";
});
echo "still the request\n";

// A registration made in a loop is the shape that says *order* rather than
// *reversal*: a queue drained backwards prints these three the other way round
// while every other line of this case still lands where it should.
array<string> $names = ["alpha", "beta", "gamma"];
foreach ($names as string $name) {
    Core\Task::afterResponse(fn (): void => {
        echo "3 reindex ", $name, "\n";
    });
}

// The last registration, made after the loop, so the queue's tail is asserted
// as well as its head.
Core\Task::afterResponse(fn (): void => {
    echo "4 cleanup\n";
});
echo "last line of the request\n";
--ORACLE--
<?php
echo "response written\n";

register_shutdown_function(function (): void {
    echo "1 receipt\n";
});
register_shutdown_function(function (): void {
    echo "2 webhook\n";
});
echo "still the request\n";

$names = ["alpha", "beta", "gamma"];
foreach ($names as $name) {
    register_shutdown_function(function () use ($name): void {
        echo "3 reindex ", $name, "\n";
    });
}

register_shutdown_function(function (): void {
    echo "4 cleanup\n";
});
echo "last line of the request\n";
